{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>And the men, those who brought forth an evil report, died.</b> The meaning — they, the bringers forth of the evil report, died, as it says (Psalms 9:17): ״בְּפֹעַל כַּפָּיו נוֹקֵשׁ רָשָׁע״ (the wicked is ensnared in the work of his own hands). It further intends to give a reason why they died by the plague: because they brought forth an evil report about the land — measure for measure. They spoke an evil thing, and HaShem struck them with דֶבֶר (plague)." "<b>Before HaShem.</b> The meaning: the glory of HaShem stood there before their departure, and it is an extraordinary permission that was granted to the destroyer here, [different] from the permission granted when the anger of HaShem burned against Aaron and Miriam — for leprosy did not afflict them until he [Aaron] had departed, whereas here permission to smite the enemies of HaShem was granted in His very presence."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {1 "The wordplay at the end depends on the root דב״ר: they דִּבְּרוּ דָבָר רַע and were struck with דֶבֶר."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:09:33.917872319Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}